    "type": "question",
    "label": "29",
    "prompt": "Factorise $x^4+1$ by interpreting using the difference of two squares.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$(x^2-\\sqrt2x+1)(x^2+\\sqrt2x+1)$.\n\nAdd and subtract $2x^2$ to form $(x^2+1)^2-(\\sqrt2x)^2$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^4+1&=x^4+2x^2+1-2x^2\\\\x^4+1&=(x^2+1)^2-(\\sqrt2x)^2\\\\x^4+1&=(x^2+1-\\sqrt2x)(x^2+1+\\sqrt2x)\\\\x^4+1&=(x^2-\\sqrt2x+1)(x^2+\\sqrt2x+1).\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 32
  },
